WEBVTT

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:11.000
<b>Long ago, demons existed in this world...</b>

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:11.000
<b>Long ago, demons existed in this world...</b>

00:00:11.390 --> 00:00:15.230
<i>Faced with monsters 
immune to modern weaponry,</i>

00:00:15.560 --> 00:00:18.540
<i>humanity was pushed to 
the brink of extinction.</i>

00:00:18.910 --> 00:00:20.620
Dear God, please...

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:23.380
Please save us.

00:00:23.380 --> 00:00:26.640
<b>Thus, gods appeared.</b>

00:00:23.380 --> 00:00:26.640
<b>Thus, gods appeared.</b>

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:29.140
<i>They were battle deities called Idaten.</i>

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:37.100
<i>They arrived suddenly, 
defeating the demons...</i>

00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:41.270
Give it a rest.

00:00:43.240 --> 00:00:44.530
<i>...and then sealing them away.</i>

00:00:45.610 --> 00:00:49.190
<i>These events occurred over 800 years ago.</i>

00:00:49.190 --> 00:00:54.330
Grandfather! Why do you all 
have to sacrifice yourselves?!

00:00:54.330 --> 00:00:57.460
There's no other way to ensure 
the seal is effective.

00:00:57.860 --> 00:01:02.960
We will travel to the other side, 
souls and all, and become part of it.

00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:04.990
Rin, you're still young.

00:01:04.990 --> 00:01:06.710
Keep living and watch over the seal.

00:01:06.710 --> 00:01:10.930
Share your strength with the gods
 who have yet to be born.

00:01:11.790 --> 00:01:16.810
And if anything happens to the seal, 
it's your job to deal with it.

00:01:16.810 --> 00:01:17.940
Don't forget that!

00:01:17.940 --> 00:01:20.860
No... No!

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:23.840
We're counting on you, Rin.

00:01:24.360 --> 00:01:25.590
Goodbye.

00:01:32.110 --> 00:01:38.390
No! Grandfather!

00:01:47.160 --> 00:01:53.050
<b><i>The Idaten Deities
</i>\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hKnow Only Peace</b>

00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:09.960
<b><i>The Idaten Deities
</i>\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hKnow Only Peace</b>

00:03:12.580 --> 00:03:16.460
<b>#1
Peacetime</b>

00:03:25.030 --> 00:03:27.340
Wh-What was that sudden gust?

00:03:27.340 --> 00:03:29.100
Gosh, that really startled me...

00:03:29.460 --> 00:03:34.850
Is it just me, or did it feel more like
 <i>something</i> blew by rather than just wind?

00:03:34.850 --> 00:03:38.330
Hey, didn't we just pass some humans?

00:03:38.640 --> 00:03:39.740
Never you mind.

00:03:39.740 --> 00:03:41.230
There's no way they saw us.

00:03:41.230 --> 00:03:43.400
Focus more on moving faster, Hayato.

00:03:44.780 --> 00:03:47.780
D-Damn it! Get back here!

00:03:47.780 --> 00:03:50.410
You hag in a kid's body!

00:04:13.020 --> 00:04:15.780
Nine hours for a lap around the earth...

00:04:16.090 --> 00:04:18.700
That's much slower than you usually manage.

00:04:18.700 --> 00:04:19.980
Are you slacking?

00:04:19.980 --> 00:04:24.440
Did you forget the part where you beat 
the shit out of me, you senile old bitch?!

00:04:26.800 --> 00:04:29.110
What arrogance when you're still half-baked.

00:04:29.110 --> 00:04:32.410
Do you think that'll help 
you become a proper Idaten?

00:04:32.410 --> 00:04:35.360
What exactly is a "proper" 
Idaten supposed to be anyway?

00:04:35.360 --> 00:04:37.660
How does being fast even matter?

00:04:37.660 --> 00:04:42.410
You drag me out here every day, 
work me to the bone... And for what?

00:04:46.190 --> 00:04:51.370
In the old days, endless hordes 
of monsters ran rampant across the land.

00:04:51.920 --> 00:04:54.740
We are deities called forth to do battle.

00:04:54.740 --> 00:04:58.020
We used our speed to fight, and—

00:04:56.730 --> 00:05:00.360
Yeah, yeah, I've heard this story.

00:05:00.690 --> 00:05:04.330
But it's been eighty years since 
I popped up in this world.

00:05:04.330 --> 00:05:06.280
And when were these monsters sealed away?

00:05:06.910 --> 00:05:08.900
About 800 years ago.

00:05:08.900 --> 00:05:12.900
See? So when's this seal busting open?

00:05:12.900 --> 00:05:15.660
The world looks peaceful enough to me.

00:05:16.070 --> 00:05:17.200
Where are you going?

00:05:17.200 --> 00:05:20.880
To have some fun. 
I've hit my training quota for the day.

00:05:20.880 --> 00:05:22.500
What's the problem?

00:05:26.600 --> 00:05:32.140
Grandfather, it seems like 800 
years of peace was too long...

00:05:39.780 --> 00:05:41.810
Hey, sorry about the holdup, Ysley.

00:05:42.780 --> 00:05:45.060
You're as swift as ever, Hayato.

00:05:45.060 --> 00:05:48.430
Not as swift as old Rin, though...

00:05:48.430 --> 00:05:50.190
Well, she's a freak of nature.

00:05:50.190 --> 00:05:52.740
I'll still outdo her one day.

00:05:53.150 --> 00:05:58.290
All you ever do is read those human books. 
Would it kill you to train a little?

00:05:58.680 --> 00:06:02.000
I'd really rather not. I'd die.

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:03.750
Besides...

00:06:04.110 --> 00:06:06.040
I love studying.

00:06:06.040 --> 00:06:11.510
And I'm able to learn more than 
any human can in their limited lifespan.

00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:15.760
Since the world's at peace, what's the 
harm in having an Idaten like that?

00:06:15.760 --> 00:06:19.290
Hey, I'm not the old bag, 
so I've got no problem with it.

00:06:19.850 --> 00:06:22.250
Come on. Let's go see what Paula's doing.

00:06:37.410 --> 00:06:42.410
Jeez, couldn't you guys be a little quieter?
 You scared them all away!

00:06:42.410 --> 00:06:46.670
We're not you. We can't run 
like dainty princesses.

00:06:47.310 --> 00:06:50.600
Did the birds tell you anything interesting?

00:06:51.740 --> 00:06:52.880
Come to think of it,

00:06:52.880 --> 00:06:56.730
they said there's a bunch of humans 
gathering by the glaciers up north.

00:06:56.730 --> 00:06:59.240
What the hell are the humans doing there?

00:06:59.240 --> 00:07:01.180
How am I supposed to know?

00:07:01.180 --> 00:07:04.120
They mentioned giant green birds, too.

00:07:04.120 --> 00:07:06.600
But those are probably airplanes.

00:07:06.920 --> 00:07:10.190
Sounds like a military transport
 for the Zoble Empire.

00:07:10.190 --> 00:07:11.980
When you say Zoble...

00:07:12.370 --> 00:07:13.980
You mean the weaponized industrial country

00:07:13.980 --> 00:07:16.880
whose air and water have gone to shit?

00:07:16.880 --> 00:07:18.980
What does their military 
want in a glacial region?

00:07:18.980 --> 00:07:19.910
No clue.

00:07:20.270 --> 00:07:22.990
It'll be faster to go see 
than stand around and guess.

00:07:22.990 --> 00:07:26.880
It's only 400 kilometers away. 
Even you two can make that in 20 minutes.

00:07:28.710 --> 00:07:30.150
I guess we should get going.

00:07:30.150 --> 00:07:31.150
You're right.

00:07:42.880 --> 00:07:45.950
<i>That sure is a lot of humans...</i>

00:07:46.610 --> 00:07:47.370
Hayato!

00:07:48.780 --> 00:07:50.150
How are things looking?

00:07:50.150 --> 00:07:51.440
Hey, you made it.

00:07:51.980 --> 00:07:56.780
I dunno what they're after, 
but that's a hell of a lot of security.

00:07:57.250 --> 00:07:59.460
Whatever they want is probably over there,

00:07:59.460 --> 00:08:03.040
but with this many people, 
I can't get closer without them noticing.

00:08:03.040 --> 00:08:05.490
Then could you check it out, Paula?

00:08:05.900 --> 00:08:06.750
Me?

00:08:06.750 --> 00:08:09.220
Put this in when you go.

00:08:17.820 --> 00:08:20.170
Something the matter, Dr. Obami?

00:08:20.170 --> 00:08:22.260
No, I must've imagined it.

00:08:22.260 --> 00:08:24.670
How is the thawing proceeding?

00:08:24.670 --> 00:08:28.770
It's 98 percent complete! Basically finished.

00:08:29.100 --> 00:08:32.480
<i>He'll be ready to move out 
as soon as he's awake.</i>

00:08:40.320 --> 00:08:43.240
Wh-What is this thing?

00:08:43.240 --> 00:08:47.250
One of the demons who left a blazing 
trail of carnage 800 years ago,

00:08:47.840 --> 00:08:52.160
and with a little elbow grease, he's still 
fully capable of destroying the world...

00:08:52.160 --> 00:08:54.420
Gyudo-kun the demon beast!

00:08:54.420 --> 00:09:00.430
<i>A bottom feeder as far as demons go, 
but more than a match for any human military.</i>

00:09:00.430 --> 00:09:02.480
What do you think? Is that cool, or what?

00:09:02.480 --> 00:09:08.200
And with that power under our control, 
Hotaena and Sarabael will be easy targets?

00:09:08.590 --> 00:09:11.440
Humans were never a consideration 
in the first place.

00:09:11.440 --> 00:09:16.270
The question is how the gods
 may have changed...

00:09:16.610 --> 00:09:17.380
Gods?

00:09:18.620 --> 00:09:20.140
Don't you worry about it!

00:09:20.140 --> 00:09:21.280
Right...

00:09:21.280 --> 00:09:24.180
<i>This old timer's as strange as ever.</i>

00:09:24.180 --> 00:09:27.910
<i>And how is he not cold, dressed like that?</i>

00:09:29.920 --> 00:09:33.110
So this is one of those demons that
the old bag never shuts up about...

00:09:33.700 --> 00:09:34.900
This was the worth the trip!

00:09:34.900 --> 00:09:36.680
I wouldn't be so pleased if I were you.

00:09:36.680 --> 00:09:42.160
Why not? It's just one leftover small fry.

00:09:43.200 --> 00:09:46.720
Well, I'm sure Rin-san could defeat 
it in the worst case scenario...

00:09:47.180 --> 00:09:51.660
But how does this Dr. Obami 
know about 800 years ago?

00:09:52.160 --> 00:09:54.230
About us or the name of this demon?

00:09:54.230 --> 00:09:58.230
There shouldn't be any humans left 
with that kind of knowledge...

00:09:58.230 --> 00:10:02.240
Maybe he's been kicking 
for 800 years like Granny.

00:10:03.470 --> 00:10:06.240
I mean, not that any human's capable of that.

00:10:06.240 --> 00:10:08.350
<i>It's true no human is capable of that...</i>

00:10:08.830 --> 00:10:12.250
<i>But what if this doctor isn't human?</i>

00:10:12.640 --> 00:10:15.250
<i>What if he's a surviving demon</i>

00:10:15.250 --> 00:10:17.380
<i>who's been working for eight centuries</i>

00:10:18.590 --> 00:10:21.210
<i>toward the revival of demonkind?</i>

00:10:34.680 --> 00:10:38.340
Hell, yeah! Free after 800 years!

00:10:38.340 --> 00:10:44.100
Hip hip hooray! 
Hip hip hooray! Hip hip hooray!

00:10:40.360 --> 00:10:43.460
Doctor! Is it safe to be standing here?

00:10:44.100 --> 00:10:47.560
Don't you worry. Gyudo-kun is 
pretty docile, generally speaking.

00:10:47.560 --> 00:10:50.180
As long as you don't provoke him, 
he won't attack.

00:10:50.180 --> 00:10:54.620
Though that doesn't apply to gods...

00:10:58.790 --> 00:11:00.520
Doctor! What is this?!

00:11:00.520 --> 00:11:04.420
Could the accelerated thawing 
have driven him mad?

00:11:20.220 --> 00:11:21.110
Paula!

00:11:21.440 --> 00:11:24.400
Enough! Fire at will!

00:11:27.520 --> 00:11:31.910
Stop that, you fool!
 He'll come after us next!

00:11:37.220 --> 00:11:41.010
Damn it... What's gotten into him?

00:11:44.060 --> 00:11:45.550
<i>A girl?</i>

00:12:01.330 --> 00:12:02.020
Wow!

00:12:06.910 --> 00:12:11.340
Huh, I let him have with that kick, 
but he seems to be fine.

00:12:11.340 --> 00:12:12.970
You can run if you want, y'know.

00:12:12.970 --> 00:12:17.790
And that's exactly what I'll do
 if I think we can't beat him.

00:12:17.790 --> 00:12:20.510
I'm sure of it! They must be Idaten!

00:12:20.510 --> 00:12:22.870
This is the perfect opportunity...

00:12:24.460 --> 00:12:28.770
<i>A generation of Idaten softened 
by the comfort of peacetime...</i>

00:12:28.770 --> 00:12:32.640
<i>This should be good. 
Let's see what you can manage.</i>

00:12:37.220 --> 00:12:39.810
Who are you boys? Where did you come from?!

00:12:39.810 --> 00:12:44.020
Your odds are better staying buried 
and fighting the cold, pops.

00:12:44.020 --> 00:12:45.170
You little...

00:12:46.080 --> 00:12:48.070
Who do you think you're talking to?!

00:12:48.070 --> 00:12:49.290
Ow! Hey!

00:12:52.440 --> 00:12:53.740
Why you...

00:12:53.740 --> 00:12:56.960
The hell was that for, asshole?! That hurt!

00:12:56.960 --> 00:12:58.100
What the—?!

00:12:58.540 --> 00:12:59.500
Uh, behind you!

00:13:03.460 --> 00:13:04.790
Hayato!

00:13:09.240 --> 00:13:11.510
He's probably dead.

00:13:15.490 --> 00:13:18.470
<i>An attack at the speed of sound 
that can generate a sonic boom?</i>

00:13:18.470 --> 00:13:22.390
<i>That'd be enough to demolish a tank, but...</i>

00:13:25.230 --> 00:13:26.360
Um...

00:13:31.280 --> 00:13:35.220
It's not enough to hurt Gyudo-kun.

00:13:35.220 --> 00:13:36.280
That makes two.

00:13:43.950 --> 00:13:45.370
And we're done.

00:13:45.370 --> 00:13:48.380
I must say, peace does nothing
 for resilience...

00:14:01.560 --> 00:14:03.620
What?! Impossible!

00:14:03.620 --> 00:14:06.600
His heart was gouged out!

00:14:10.980 --> 00:14:13.230
<i>He's not very fast.</i>

00:14:13.230 --> 00:14:15.690
<i>If we focus on evasion, 
we should easily be able to escape.</i>

00:14:17.590 --> 00:14:21.240
<i>It's like he's only attacking 
Idaten on instinct.</i>

00:14:21.700 --> 00:14:25.960
<i>Lashing out at us, before anything else,
 after being thawed out...</i>

00:14:25.960 --> 00:14:29.000
<i>That suggests the cognitive 
capacity of an insect.</i>

00:14:29.760 --> 00:14:32.010
What's going on here?!

00:14:32.010 --> 00:14:37.600
<i>Was it some kind of trick? Or is piercing 
their hearts not enough to kill them?!</i>

00:14:39.780 --> 00:14:40.920
Ysley?

00:14:40.920 --> 00:14:42.110
You're awake?

00:14:42.110 --> 00:14:44.400
Whoa, you're injured! Are you okay?!

00:14:45.580 --> 00:14:48.500
It does hurt pretty badly, 
so can you stand on your own?

00:14:49.620 --> 00:14:51.840
It only hurts? You're not gonna die?

00:14:51.840 --> 00:14:54.860
You'll understand if you ever 
get your heart gouged out.

00:14:54.860 --> 00:14:58.320
More importantly, this exchange 
has made three things clear.

00:14:58.940 --> 00:15:03.680
First, that monster is incredibly 
tough and powerful,

00:15:03.680 --> 00:15:06.640
but it can't compare to us 
Idaten in terms of speed.

00:15:06.640 --> 00:15:08.670
If we need to flee, 
that shouldn't be a problem.

00:15:09.200 --> 00:15:10.840
Second...

00:15:11.540 --> 00:15:15.570
It seems the good doctor 
doesn't know much about us,

00:15:15.570 --> 00:15:19.340
considering how surprised he was that 
I survived having my heart pierced...

00:15:19.340 --> 00:15:21.990
That surprised me, too!

00:15:21.990 --> 00:15:24.640
I suppose it would.

00:15:24.640 --> 00:15:27.310
To be honest, the first time
 I had my heart pulped

00:15:27.310 --> 00:15:30.500
and my neck broken, 
I thought I was a goner, too...

00:15:35.890 --> 00:15:38.240
What's this? An earthquake?

00:15:38.240 --> 00:15:43.490
As for the third thing,
 that monster is strong.

00:15:43.500 --> 00:15:44.200
However...

00:15:48.000 --> 00:15:51.330
You think I'm gonna let that slide, 
you piece of shit?!

00:15:51.330 --> 00:15:53.460
Hope you're ready for payback a millionfold!

00:15:53.460 --> 00:15:57.120
Hayato, who has been training 
with Rin-san for 80 years,

00:15:57.120 --> 00:15:58.760
should have no problem fighting him.

00:15:59.470 --> 00:16:01.480
Eat this!

00:16:10.980 --> 00:16:11.870
Hey.

00:16:13.230 --> 00:16:17.030
You left your body wide open,
 you beefy dumbass!

00:16:27.000 --> 00:16:29.210
Nice! Get him, Hayato!

00:16:36.030 --> 00:16:38.920
He's nothing like the one in glasses.

00:16:38.920 --> 00:16:41.690
This doesn't look good...

00:17:04.200 --> 00:17:07.420
Okay! On your feet, big boy!

00:17:07.420 --> 00:17:09.580
This time, I'm blowing your head clean off—

00:17:13.140 --> 00:17:14.980
What? Is he dead?

00:17:22.090 --> 00:17:23.590
<i>He </i>is<i> dead...</i>

00:17:24.200 --> 00:17:29.350
<i>Immediate death following destructive 
organ trauma is a trait of organisms.</i>

00:17:29.970 --> 00:17:33.850
<i>Meaning demons are closer 
to living creatures than us Idaten...</i>

00:17:37.570 --> 00:17:40.230
I wasn't able to retrieve Gyudo-kun,

00:17:40.230 --> 00:17:43.820
but I've obtained data that more 
than makes up for that loss.

00:17:44.150 --> 00:17:46.570
<i>Now, you'll have to excuse 
me as I make my exit.</i>

00:17:46.910 --> 00:17:50.510
<i>Farewell to you, new generation of Idaten!</i>

00:17:52.530 --> 00:17:53.410
That's...

00:17:53.410 --> 00:17:55.220
the new high-speed VTOL fighter jet

00:17:55.300 --> 00:17:57.730
that can maintain a cruising speed of Mach 2!

00:17:59.170 --> 00:18:01.670
Although, that said...

00:18:02.310 --> 00:18:04.090
Wh-What... What was that?

00:18:04.090 --> 00:18:04.800
Yo.

00:18:04.800 --> 00:18:06.090
Yo, <i>what</i>?!

00:18:06.090 --> 00:18:09.100
It can't escape Hayato.

00:18:09.100 --> 00:18:12.180
All right, Gramps, quit panicking.

00:18:12.180 --> 00:18:14.560
Let's land this thing and have a little chat.

00:18:15.090 --> 00:18:16.190
Here we go...

00:18:16.190 --> 00:18:18.690
S-Stop! Don't do anything drastic!

00:18:25.640 --> 00:18:28.060
Wait, humans die from falls, right?

00:18:29.110 --> 00:18:31.080
Did I do that wrong?

00:18:33.720 --> 00:18:35.910
Hey, Gramps?

00:18:35.910 --> 00:18:37.570
You still alive?

00:18:42.240 --> 00:18:46.800
Say, Ysley, how long are you 
going to study that dead monster?

00:18:48.390 --> 00:18:50.080
Huh? Ysley?

00:18:50.950 --> 00:18:53.060
The monster's body is gone, too...

00:18:53.890 --> 00:18:56.670
Yes, that's right. A dead monster specimen.

00:18:56.990 --> 00:18:58.810
Retrieve it as quickly as possible, please.

00:18:59.300 --> 00:19:01.630
It's near where we first found it.

00:19:01.630 --> 00:19:04.780
I'll send the specific 
coordinates in a moment.

00:19:05.180 --> 00:19:07.030
Listen, you need to hurry.

00:19:07.960 --> 00:19:10.030
Don't let Zoble get it first.

00:19:12.030 --> 00:19:15.040
Damn you, boy...

00:19:15.040 --> 00:19:17.040
I can't believe you wrecked it!

00:19:17.040 --> 00:19:20.160
Do you realize how much of a pain
 it is to fix these bodies?!

00:19:20.160 --> 00:19:25.270
You doof! Dunce! Dumb-dumb! 
Stupid, stupid stupidhead!

00:19:21.420 --> 00:19:24.120
So you're a robot, Gramps?

00:19:24.120 --> 00:19:29.680
Man, Ysley is gonna have a lot 
of fun taking you apart.

00:19:25.270 --> 00:19:27.540
Big old stupid stupidhead!

00:19:30.590 --> 00:19:32.950
You think this is a game, boy?!

00:19:32.950 --> 00:19:35.820
Try this on for size! The device all men 
dream about making use of...

00:19:33.680 --> 00:19:37.940
<b>Self-Destruct</b>

00:19:35.820 --> 00:19:37.000
A self-destruct switch!

00:19:37.000 --> 00:19:37.940
And a-boop!

00:19:43.500 --> 00:19:45.650
Damn, guess he's a goner...

00:20:04.960 --> 00:20:07.420
Well, we're in for a treat.

00:20:07.420 --> 00:20:09.220
She sure doesn't look like an old lady...

00:20:10.080 --> 00:20:12.520
What are you men thinking?!

00:20:12.520 --> 00:20:16.750
You must realize God will not 
forgive this kind of pillaging!

00:20:17.750 --> 00:20:21.020
When the world was on the 
verge of destruction,

00:20:21.020 --> 00:20:23.250
God the creator descended from Heaven

00:20:23.250 --> 00:20:26.190
and brought salvation to 
the world and its people!

00:20:26.530 --> 00:20:31.060
What you're doing is blasphemy 
in the eyes of our merciful—

00:20:35.540 --> 00:20:37.900
God? What's that?

00:20:37.900 --> 00:20:39.540
Tissues work better than 
blessings for sneezes!

00:20:39.540 --> 00:20:42.280
They've got other uses, too...

00:20:42.280 --> 00:20:44.670
Well, God, we're gonna help ourselves.

00:20:44.670 --> 00:20:46.020
O Lord...

00:21:13.570 --> 00:21:16.410
<i>Dear Lord, please...</i>

00:21:17.210 --> 00:21:21.300
<i>Please... grant us salvation...</i>

00:21:22.220 --> 00:21:23.490
<i>God!</i>
